      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "id": "note-1h9oay7d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 740,
      "y": 404,
      "width": 1415.7,
      "height": 146.25,
      "strokeColor": "#e8590c",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "text": "Same author action.\nSame topic. Same worker.\n\nThe two paths diverge on\nONE follower-count check —\nand that single branch is\nwhat stops a 40M-follower\naccount from issuing 40M\nRedis writes per tweet.",
      "originalText": "Same author action.\nSame topic. Same worker.\n\nThe two paths diverge on\nONE follower-count check —\nand that single branch is\nwhat stops a 40M-follower\naccount from issuing 40M\nRedis writes per tweet.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1660989106,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2101091945,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1735689600000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "id": "note-sdlpwhw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 740,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 2660.625,
      "height": 62.5,
      "strokeColor": "#5c5f66",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "text": "Why it balances: you follow thousands of ordinary accounts but only a handful of celebrities, so the read-side merge stays small —\nwhile celebrities are rare, so skipping their fan-out removes most of the write cost. The two asymmetries cancel out.\n\nWhat it costs: two code paths to keep consistent, and an explicit backfill when an account crosses the 10k threshold in either direction.",
      "originalText": "Why it balances: you follow thousands of ordinary accounts but only a handful of celebrities, so the read-side merge stays small —\nwhile celebrities are rare, so skipping their fan-out removes most of the write cost. The two asymmetries cancel out.\n\nWhat it costs: two code paths to keep consistent, and an explicit backfill when an account crosses the 10k threshold in either direction.",
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
